@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 19 and 20"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.15.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage/1.15.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch19ch20_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.15.0 (2026-11-16): Chapter 20 page 9.98.0 on template 9.53.4 and its checks."@en .

ex:TK8_BuildPage_Ch20 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Page 9.98.0 (03-materials/ch20/page/sen0414_ch20_page_v9_98_0.html, template 9.53.4, page-data builder 2.28.0, page builder 4.18.3) built from the lambda-free A-box 1.0.3 (08-tooling/ch20-page/abox_lambda_free_make_v1_0_0.py: 57 inputs rewritten, each run next to its original and equal, 0 lambda left), the six stories of the deck (sen0414_ch20_stories_v1_0_1.py replaces the Gmail launch story with the IMAP story) with their pictures, and the chapter-code manifest 1.0.1. Page data recorded under Python 3.13.18; the concept examples that need ezgmail or a local mail server stay recorded, not run (as before). Chapter code tab: 19 examples in slide order; in the browser 11 run and equal the slide, 8 (ezgmail and aiosmtpd examples) show the result recorded on the slide, marked as recorded, not run (new in template 9.53.4, with the reason from the manifest); the subprocess stand-in of the Chapter 19 page runs the last one. Two repairs made on the way, both new versions: the material check 1.0.1 reads the page's JSON escapes (1.0.0 reported 4 frames missing that are present, checked by a separate program on all 19 examples); template 9.53.4 caps a story photograph at 45 percent of the screen height (the portrait phone picture filled the whole screen on a laptop) and no longer prints the labels WHO, WHERE and WHEN in the Stories tab (the standing storytelling rule), which required page test 9.39.0 (new file over 9.38.0; its one change is that fact-row expectation). The Chapter 19 page still carries the labels, because it was built on 9.53.3: a correction of that page belongs to the correction step after closure." .
ex:TK8_BuildVerify_Ch20 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Logs in 08-tooling/ch20-page/logs_v9_98_0: material check 8 of 8 pass; manifest self-check pass (19 examples, deck code equals manifest code, every example re-run alone and in order); story layout pass at every viewport; page test 9.39.0 ran 70 features, 70 passed, 0 failed (including Code Lab: 21 of 21 concept examples the same). NOT VERIFIED: the page test crashes the browser tab in its phone-size step (tab sparql, test line 850) on every run, so the checks after that step did not run, among them the chapter-code step of the test (my own browser run of all 19 chapter examples is in the probe files and shows 11 run and match, 8 recorded), phone and tablet layout, the accessibility scan of the later panes, the light theme, the sideways-scroll check and the audit zip. Same crash as on the Chapter 18 and Chapter 19 pages. Root cause searched and not found: the browser flags --disable-gpu and --disable-dev-shm-usage change nothing (page_test_probe_flags.log), and a phone-size loop over all 38 tabs in a fresh browser, with the page's examples run beforehand, does not crash (crash_probe_tabprobe.py, crash_probe_memprobe.py), so the crash needs something the earlier steps of the test leave behind. Carried into the closure report as a missing item. Verification was done by the same agent that built the page, so it is not independent." .
ex:ST8_BuildCh20 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck 2.0.0, page 9.98.0 and their checks done; the unverified remainder of the page test and the missing reviewed conditions are recorded on the verify tasks." .
